{"seconds": 50.7, "exit": 0, "final": "After Kg6, Re6+ drives the king further. The key line is clear:\n\n**1. Qxg7+! Kxg7 2. Re7+ (attacking f7 and b7) and White wins material on f7 or b7 with overwhelming advantage.**\n\nThis is a classic tactic: queen sacrifice to open up the king, then rook checks force the king into a mating net or lead to material gain.\n\n**Best move: Qxg7+**\n\n**Main line:** Qxg7+ Kxg7 Re7+ Kh7 Rxf7+ Kg8 (or Kg6/Kh6) and White dominates with queen and rook vs rooks and bishop, having won the bishop and with the king exposed.\n\n**Motif: Sacrifice** (queen sacrifice opening the king)\n\n**Coaching note:** The queen sacrifice Qxg7+ opens up Black's king on the back rank. After forced Kxg7, the rook checks from e7 force the king around the board while White wins material (the bishop on f7) and achieves a winning position. Always scan for forcing sequences: check can become a powerful weapon when the opponent's king loses shelter.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxg7+\", \"line\": [\"Qxg7+\", \"Kxg7\", \"Re7+\", \"Kh7\", \"Rxf7+\", \"Kg8\"], \"motifs\": [\"sacrifice\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "square": "f2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "square": "g4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "square": "f7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1